Redraw the whole Amiga screen after a state restore.

FS-UAE redraws only the display lines whose Amiga content changed since the
previous frame, and nothing marks the screen lost when a state is restored, so
after a load the picture stays black until the game draws each line again.
Applies to grahambates/fs-uae, branch remote_debugger_barto, at b70b1180.

diff --git a/src/savestate.cpp b/src/savestate.cpp
index ced6c9f..7dbe31b 100644
--- a/src/savestate.cpp
+++ b/src/savestate.cpp
@@ -1014,6 +1014,7 @@ bool savestate_restore_finish(void)
 	savestate_state = 0;
 	init_hz_normal();
 	audio_activate();
+	notice_screen_contents_lost(0);
 #ifdef FSUAE
     uae_callback(uae_on_restore_state_finished, savestate_fname);
 #endif
